    #      directory that sample's phase recorded (P1's, P2's, P3's two), for the
    #      same workbook and label; the tool's line, the diff table and the
    #      entries table the same; the summary the same but for its two measured
    #      columns (wall_s, peak_rss_kb);
    #   4. the run log's own comparisons (namescmp.py, linkscmp.py, propscmp.py
    #      and protectcmp.py, python3, zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree,
    #      printed below) over every output of both labels, a planted control per
    #      flag; protectcmp.py's hash flag reads the output (F9) and linkscmp.py
    #      takes its two forms from W's own relationship (F10);
    #   5. P2 verification ruling 8's retag plant on a byte-built workbook whose
    #      root binds no relationships prefix, kept, with linkscmp.py's F10 form
    #      shown read from the workbook's rels part;
    #   6. each record pair checked against its run directory, and its entries
    #      and xml tables against the phase record's;
    #   7. the keep regenerated on both targets, compared, and against P3's
    #      committed open-check record; the edit open check over the host keep,
    #      recorded as m2p4a-open-<utc-date>-<shortsha>;
    #   8. this script's own standard error counted (specs/0017 P1 verification
    #      ruling 7).
    # No value, text, sheet name, reference, target or part name from the corpus
    # is printed.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M2 part 4a P4 from P3's run script (printed in
    # records/logs/m2p4a-p3/run.log; its change list AV to AZ is there, with P2's
    # AO to AU and P1's AE to AN before it), and from part 3 P4's run script
    # (printed in records/logs/m2p3-p4/run.log, changes X to AD), which reran
    # every sample with the size log's binaries. What differs, and why:
    #  BA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4a-p4/scripts, on the disk),
    #      the build directory (m2p4a-p4/run) and the keep (m2p4a-p4/keep-host)
    #      are this phase's; the base is P3's record commit ("M2 part 4a P3
    #      record:"), also the last to add an open-check record; the phase
    #      commit is the probe commit by its subject; the record stems are
    #      m2p4a-p4-<sample>-.
    #  BB. No release build: the binaries are size.log's ("P4": "the release
    #      binaries the size log hashed"), run where size.log built them,
    #      <sizebuild>/target, each hashed and compared with its hash: line in
    #      size.log (part 3 P4's change Y). size.log is the third argument;
    #      <sizebuild> is the input RUN_SIZE_BUILD, by default
    #      <home>/.cache/emend-build/m2p4a-p4/size, and joins the labelled input
    #      lines.
    #  BC. Four samples, four run directories: each output compared by sha256
    #      with the phase run directory's, found from the phase's record commit
    #      by its subject and the run directory its corpus record .md names,
    #      checked against the name planning gave for it, its run row's commit
    #      checked against the record commit's parent and its tool_args against
    #      the sample (part 3 P4's change Z). The summary is compared without
    #      wall_s and peak_rss_kb; the entries table, each diff table and each
    #      tool line byte for byte.
    #  BD. The record check is part 3 P4's (change AA): the tables against the
    #      run directory, the family tables counted from them, the entries and
